# Data-Driven Evidence-Based Syntactic Sugar Design - Artifact README

## Purpose
This artifact is designed to reproduce the tables presented in the ICSE'24 technical track paper "Data-Driven Evidence-Based Syntactic Sugar Design." The authors are applying for the "Available" badge since the artifact is made publicly available on Zenodo. Additionally, the authors are applying for the "Reusable" badge as they provide scripts to reproduce the results presented in their paper.

## Provenance
The publicly available artifact can be found on Zenodo ([https://zenodo.org/records/10460716](https://zenodo.org/records/10460716)).

The artifact mines data which was mined from GitHub using the Boa language and infrastructure ([https://boa.cs.iastate.edu/boa/](https://boa.cs.iastate.edu/boa/)).

Specifically, the [2019 Java dataset](https://boa.cs.iastate.edu/boa/?q=content/dataset-notes-october-2019) is mined in this study.

The following Boa public jobs were ran for this study, the following links provide the script ran and the results of the job:

- [https://boa.cs.iastate.edu/boa/index.php?q=boa/job/102419](https://boa.cs.iastate.edu/boa/index.php?q=boa/job/102419)
- [https://boa.cs.iastate.edu/boa/index.php?q=boa/job/102421](https://boa.cs.iastate.edu/boa/index.php?q=boa/job/102421)
- [https://boa.cs.iastate.edu/boa/index.php?q=boa/job/102492](https://boa.cs.iastate.edu/boa/index.php?q=boa/job/102492)
- [https://boa.cs.iastate.edu/boa/index.php?q=boa/job/102494](https://boa.cs.iastate.edu/boa/index.php?q=boa/job/102494)
- [https://boa.cs.iastate.edu/boa/index.php?q=boa/job/102513](https://boa.cs.iastate.edu/boa/index.php?q=boa/job/102513)
- [https://boa.cs.iastate.edu/boa/index.php?q=boa/job/102545](https://boa.cs.iastate.edu/boa/index.php?q=boa/job/102545)
- [https://boa.cs.iastate.edu/boa/index.php?q=boa/job/102443](https://boa.cs.iastate.edu/boa/index.php?q=boa/job/102443)
- [https://boa.cs.iastate.edu/boa/index.php?q=boa/job/102454](https://boa.cs.iastate.edu/boa/index.php?q=boa/job/102454)
- [https://boa.cs.iastate.edu/boa/index.php?q=boa/job/102563](https://boa.cs.iastate.edu/boa/index.php?q=boa/job/102563)
- [https://boa.cs.iastate.edu/boa/index.php?q=boa/job/102565](https://boa.cs.iastate.edu/boa/index.php?q=boa/job/102565)

## Data
The artifact is organized as such:

- **Kotlin-Desugars-Mined:**
  - Provides Boa scripts used to mine Java equivalents of unimplemented syntactic sugars.
  - A "results.csv" file contains the output and link to the relevant Boa job which gathered this data.

- **Subgraph-Data:**
  - Provides data for 3 tasks mined in the paper:
    - Mining subgraphs which motivate new language features ("new")
    - Mining subgraphs from a sampled data ("small")
    - Mining subgraphs from pretty-printed AST data ("pretty")
  - Data in this folder contains the raw data mined from Boa ("0-raw"), and the filtered and labeled subgraph data for each task ("1-filtered"). The subgraphs that motivate the 7 syntactic sugars explored in our paper are also provided ("2-presented-sugars-subgraphs").

- **Survey:**
  - Provides the anonymized data resulting from the conducted survey.

- **Tables:**
  - Provides Python scripts to reproduce the tables from the paper.

## Setup (for executable artifacts)
The only hard requirement is Python 3 with pandas.  Install required Python packages with:

> pip install -r requirements.txt

## Usage (for executable artifacts)
To reproduce the tables presented in the paper, run the script found at `Tables/reproduce-tables.py`. This will overwrite any pre-existing versions of the outputted tables for others to manually verify that the output matches the results presented in the paper.

## License
An MIT [LICENSE](./LICENSE) is included in this replication package.
